# gb_power module requirements (reference; already merged into C:\GB-x86\inject\native\modules\modules.load(.late), k12).
# gbinit / gb_modules.sh pass the words after the file name to insmod as module parameters.
# modules.load (gbinit, before Android init):
crc-itu-t.ko
surface_aggregator.ko
surface_aggregator_registry.ko
surface_aggregator_hub.ko
# scope_device=1 needs kernel patch 0001 (in k12); an unpatched module ignores it ("unknown parameter ... ignored") and
# gb_power falls back to hiding BAT1/BAT2 with a bind mount.
surface_battery.ko scope_device=1
surface_charger.ko
surface_dtx.ko
surface_gpe.ko
surface_hotplug.ko
# test_power must be loaded before the health HAL scans /sys/class/power_supply ("on boot"); any position in
# modules.load satisfies that. Patch 0002 (in k12) adds battery_charge_full/_design/battery_temp.
test_power.ko
# modules.load.late (gb_modules.sh, early-init, after it modprobes lapis's own platform_profile from /vendor/lib/modules,
# which also serves lapis's processor_thermal): do NOT ship/load our platform_profile.ko.
#   surface_platform_profile.ko
# NOT natively: ac.ko / battery.ko (VM-only ACPI battery) - they would add more Battery/Mains supplies.
